      "writtenOn": "2022-02-03T00:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the assumption here is that the internal config captures the \u0027flags\u0027 that\nare set in the named-gpios child nodes.\nThere\u0027s a little bit of a mismatch here with Zephyr, in that struct gpio_dt_spec flags only provide 8 bits, which indicate the physical pin characteristics.\nGPIO_INPUT and GPIO_OUTPUT are set as \u0027extra\u0027 flags in gpio_pin_configure_dt, which\nor\u0027s in the 8 bits of saved flags.\nSo if you *are* using named-gpios, then the GPIOs get initialised anyway, so this is redundant. If you want to make the code independent of named-gpios (which is likely a good thing), then you won\u0027t have all the flags, and you need to explicitly init the GPIO with the extra flags like INPUT/OUTPUT etc.",
      "revId": "d9178582d3242d155cb8bae1e9d9f08b1df4bdd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
